      {
         "id": "SECTION_rules",
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "### General rules\n\nThe game has three levels. On the left, a multiplication appears; on the right, its result is shown with groups of characters. Each rectangle on the right holds as many characters as the first factor, and the number of rectangles is the second factor. For example, 2 × 4 shows two characters in each of four rectangles.\n\nIn the first level, three multiplications appear: one is from the 0 times table and two are from the 1 times table. In the second level, two multiplications appear, both from the 2 times table. In the third level, two multiplications appear, both from the 3 times table. Select a multiplication and then its result; if the pair is correct, both stay highlighted. When you match every pair, you complete the level and can move on to the next one.",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ]
      },
      {
         "id": "SECTION_game",
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "### The Game\n\nMatch each multiplication on the left with its result on the right. The result is also shown as groups of characters, so you can count them to check your answer.",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
